From 927e6d52e6828011f6f8a14212298daf0f15c8dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: XiaoShao <26596822+xiaoshao9704@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 00:35:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] hearth patch 1: drop EnableSped (fork-only pion API) so
 the server builds against upstream pion

EnableSped only exists in livekit's -warp pion fork. It is gated by EnableWarp
(default off), so removing the call changes nothing in the default configuration
and lets the whole server compile against upstream pion/webrtc, pion/ice and
pion/dtls. EnableSctpSnap in the same guard exists upstream and is kept.
---
 pkg/rtc/transport.go | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/pkg/rtc/transport.go b/pkg/rtc/transport.go
index a28ea20f..d300a573 100644
--- a/pkg/rtc/transport.go
+++ b/pkg/rtc/transport.go
@@ -384,7 +384,6 @@ func newPeerConnection(
 	}
 
 	if params.EnableWarp {
-		se.EnableSped(true)
 		se.EnableSctpSnap(true)
 	}
 
